# SSH client config, symlinked to ~/.ssh/config by install.sh. This replaces
# the ~/.ssh/config the README used to have you write by hand.
#
# Specific hosts come first on purpose: ssh keeps the *first* value it sees for
# each keyword, so a `Host *` block below can supply defaults but can never
# override anything set above it. Put a new host under the wildcard and its
# User will be silently ignored.
#
# Usernames differ per machine, which is the whole reason this file exists --
# `ssh gengar.local` from shellder is qtbt, the reverse is yellott. Who is
# *allowed* to log in where is ssh/authorized_keys; this file only says who to
# log in as.
#
# butterfree is deliberately absent: I have not confirmed its short username,
# and a wrong guess here fails more confusingly than no entry at all.

Host gengar gengar.local
  User qtbt

Host shellder shellder.local
  User yellott

Host *
  AddKeysToAgent yes
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
